# sqlx records a SHA-384 checksum over the raw bytes of every migration file
# at compile time. Line-ending conversion changes those bytes, and an existing
# database then fails with:
#   migration N was previously applied but has been modified
# Pin SQL files to CRLF so every checkout (Windows, Linux, CI) and every
# release build embeds byte-identical migrations. Do not change the line
# endings of files under crates/warfarin-db/migrations/ once shipped.
*.sql text eol=crlf
